# FITOS hosted build — build-time configuration (Phase 6.7 Gate 6.7-2).
#
# Copy to apps/mobile/hosted.env if you need to override anything; hosted.env
# is gitignored and read only by tool/hosted.ps1. Nothing here is a server
# secret: the Firebase values are the project's PUBLIC client config, and the
# API address is public. The Gemini key, database passwords and the consent
# salt live in Google Secret Manager and never in any app file.
#
# Firebase: leave these out to reuse apps/mobile/alpha.env — the hosted build
# uses the SAME Firebase project (fitos-dev-3208b), so sign-in is unchanged.
# FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# FIREBASE_APP_ID=
# FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# The hosted API. HTTPS, a DNS name, no port, no path. Leave it out to use the
# Cloud Run service's deterministic address,
#   https://fitos-api-alpha-<project number>.asia-south1.run.app
# where the project number is FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID (a Firebase
# project's sender id IS its Google Cloud project number). After the first
# deploy, confirm it with:
#   gcloud run services describe fitos-api-alpha --region asia-south1 --format='value(status.url)'
# Later: https://api.tryfitos.me (not configured yet).
# API_BASE_URL=
